WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.004
One hundred and fifty-one bills analyzed across the 45th Parliament of Canada.

00:00:04.954 --> 00:00:11.920
Ninety-four recorded divisions across twenty contentious votes — every yea and nay tracked, every party pattern documented.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.806
The data reveals razor-thin margins on critical legislation.

00:00:15.806 --> 00:00:23.147
Party voting percentages show near-total discipline on whipped votes — and the rare moments of dissent where individual MPs broke ranks.

00:00:23.147 --> 00:00:26.523
Bill categories are charted by type and outcome.

00:00:26.523 --> 00:00:29.409
The question is not whether Parliament voted.

00:00:29.409 --> 00:00:33.397
The question is whether Parliament deliberated — or simply performed.
